---
// The Leichte-Sprache switch. Prototype — see src/lib/leichteSprache.js for what it does
// and, more importantly, for what it deliberately does not do.
//
// It sits in the exercise toolbar rather than in the site nav on purpose: this is not a
// site-wide language setting like DE/EN, it is a property of the exercise you are looking
// at, and only the pages that have written both registers should offer it. A switch in the
// nav would promise it everywhere.
//
// Labelled, not an icon. "Leichte Sprache" is the term the audience for it already knows
// from Behörden and news sites; a lightbulb or an "A" would be a puzzle in front of the
// thing that exists to remove puzzles.
---
<button
  type="button"
  class="ls-switch"
  data-ls-toggle
  aria-pressed="false"
  title="Zwischen normalem Deutsch und Leichter Sprache wechseln"
>
  <span class="ls-switch-track" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ls-switch-knob"></span></span>
  <span class="ls-switch-txt">
    <span class="ls-switch-kicker">Sprache der Erklärungen</span>
    <span class="ls-switch-state" data-ls-toggle-state>Normal</span>
  </span>
</button>
